Subject: d3d11: reject operations outside the experimental backend surface

A standalone On12 device has no WineD3D device or context. The inherited
entry points must not dereference those absent objects when an application
calls an unimplemented operation. Return DXGI_ERROR_UNSUPPORTED for failing
APIs, diagnose void operations, and clear getter outputs. Restrict queried
interfaces to the base device/context and the explicit On12 interface so
video and later-version vtables cannot bypass the backend boundary. Buffer
DXGI forwarding also rejects its absent backing object. Ordinary WineD3D
objects retain their existing dispatch paths.
